From 151d6006156177a213ec2c421b4b1c35e4b741c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quinby Janes <qcj2000@columbia.edu>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:02:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Rewrite FAQ headings as simple questions and link to Learn
 pages

- Existing cards now read as questions: "Do I need a referral to genetic
  counseling?", "How much does testing cost, and does insurance cover
  it?", "Is my genetic information kept private?" (answers unchanged;
  the privacy answer now also links to Your rights & choices).
- Wallet icon replaced with a dollar sign, per Hila.
- New questions grouped under About genetic testing, Understanding
  results, Your family, and Support and research. Each gives the Learn
  page's own one-line summary and a "Read more" link instead of
  repeating the page (summaries are pulled from learnTopics.ts, so they
  stay in sync).
- Page title is now "Frequently asked questions".
- Search index refreshed for the new FAQ text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012p2rj8y1uznXf4UStSfSh8
